---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import ToolVote from '../../../components/ToolVote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Livspusslet"
  description="A household runs on a plan that lives in one person's head. Livspusslet puts the year on a page instead. Working prototype, in Swedish."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></p>
      <h1>Livspusslet</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Every household runs on a plan that lives in one person's head. This one puts the year on a page, so
        it stops being one person's job to remember it.
      </p>

      <p class="demo-open">
        <a class="demo-button" href="/tools/livspusslet-app.html">Open the clickable prototype →</a>
        <span class="demo-hint">It is an application. A big screen suits it.</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="demo-wide">
      <iframe
        id="livspusslet-demo"
        src="/tools/livspusslet-app.html"
        title="Livspusslet prototype"
        loading="lazy"
      ></iframe>
      <figure class="demo-narrow">
        <img
          src="/tools/livspusslet-demo.gif"
          alt="Livspusslet's overview: what needs attention this week, sorted by how urgent it is to act."
          loading="lazy"
          width="1366"
          height="896"
        />
        <figcaption>
          The prototype wants a wider screen than this one, so here it is as a recording.
          <a href="/tools/livspusslet-app.html">Open the real one</a> on something larger.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="demo-fallback">
        <a href="/tools/livspusslet-app.html">Open the prototype full-screen</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="block insight-page">

      <h2>What it tries to solve</h2>

      <p>
        Nothing in a household is difficult on its own. Booking the chimney sweep is not difficult. What is
        difficult is that there are two hundred of them a year, they have no shared list, and they are all
        held in the same head — usually not the head that volunteered. And most of them have a window rather
        than a date: booking the boat's winter storage in June is early, in October it is a phone call to
        somewhere already full.
      </p>

      <h2>What it does</h2>

      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>
          <strong>A rolling year, drawn as windows.</strong> Each arc starts when it is worth starting and
          ends on the last day that works, and the reminders count backwards from when preparation has to
          begin rather than from the day itself.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Chores with minutes on them.</strong> Weighted by age, so the split becomes something to
          look at together instead of argue about. The gap between what was agreed and what the log says is
          roughly the whole agenda of a family meeting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Food, holidays and money that know who lives here.</strong> Meals against each person's
          diet and training load, holiday arithmetic ranked by how many days off each vacation day buys, and a
          budget with a reference value, your own figure and the outcome side by side.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A calendar each.</strong> One feed per person that Apple, Google and Outlook subscribe to —
          their own things plus everything shared.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        It runs as a single process on your own machine. No accounts, no cloud: the whole household is two
        files you can copy to back it up.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is</h2>

      <p>
        A working prototype my own family uses. Swedish throughout — the holidays, school terms and grocery
        habits it knows are Swedish too, and an English version is a real translation job rather than a
        switch.
      </p>

      <ToolVote tool="livspusslet" />
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .insight-page h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2.6rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .demo-open {
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
  }
  .demo-hint {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .demo-hint {
      display: block;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    }
  }
  .demo-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--moss);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--moss);
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .demo-button:hover {
    background: var(--moss);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  /* The prototype is an application: it steps out of the reading column and
     keeps a viewport of its own rather than growing with its tallest tab. */
  .demo-wide {
    width: min(65rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
    margin: 2rem 0 3.4rem 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
  .demo-wide iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: min(46rem, 82vh);
    border: 1px solid var(--mist);
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .demo-narrow {
    display: none;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .demo-narrow img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--mist);
  }
  .demo-narrow figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  .demo-fallback {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .demo-wide {
      width: 100vw;
    }
    .demo-wide iframe {
      display: none;
    }
    .demo-narrow {
      display: block;
    }
    .demo-fallback {
      padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  .feature-list {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .feature-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .feature-list strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Same-origin, so the site's theme toggle can be handed through to the frame.
  const frame = document.getElementById('livspusslet-demo') as HTMLIFrameElement | null;

  if (frame) {
    const syncTheme = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc) return;
      const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
      if (theme) doc.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      else delete doc.documentElement.dataset.theme;
    };

    frame.addEventListener('load', syncTheme);
    if (frame.contentDocument?.readyState === 'complete') syncTheme();

    new MutationObserver(syncTheme).observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-theme'],
    });
  }
</script>
